Z||000005||LarryB||09-24-2001||07:42 PM||||It could be that you've got intermittent bottlenecks in the path between your machine and Cliff's web server.<P>Without getting into a technical discussion many kinds of network traffic (ftp is one most of us are familiar with, http is another) use a connection-oriented methodology; when a network packet of information is sent an acknowledgement is sent from the recipient so that the sender knows it arrived OK.  If the sender does not get an acknowledgement back within a certain period of time it will resend the information.<P>What *could* be happening is that in either direction acknowledgements aren't being received fast enough and information is being retransmitted.||||reg||1
